; Higher-order binder form — `map` over a finite vector squares each
; element. The body `(* x x)` re-evaluates once per element with `x`
; bound to the next vector entry. Validation passes (core's
; `map` / `*` declarations are in scope for top-level eval); the
; eval pass runs the binder and surfaces `[1 4 9 16]` in
; `HostResult.evaluated_results`. Zig, Web, and Rust hosts all
; assert the value via the `(values …)` block.
(map [x] [1 2 3 4] (* x x))
